# Contributor: unex <7575866+unex@users.noreply.github.com>
# Maintainer: unex <7575866+unex@users.noreply.github.com>
# The panel app program of the xx50 panels: Tessera (the touch-screen firmware
# of github.com/MaxGramser/homeassistant_espscreen) as an ESPHome host program
# with LVGL, the tsx_drm display and the tsx_evdev input. One program for every
# xx50 panel: the service tsx-panel-app of tsx-panel-app gives it the name, the
# MAC and the API key of the panel at start. The classic panel app (tsx_cards,
# esphome-lvgl/ of tsx-xx50-linux) is not packaged.
#
# Source: the release asset tsx-xx50-panel-app-src-$pkgver.tar.gz of the tag
# v$pkgver of tsx-xx50-linux. release.yml makes it with tessera/build.sh and
# tessera/mksource.sh: ESPHome writes the C++ project of Tessera and of
# panel-app/esphome of tsx-linux-common (the tag in COMMON_REF). BUILDINFO in
# the archive names the versions and the commits. The archive has the
# corresponding source of the program (docs/tessera.md "License" of
# tsx-xx50-linux): the project, the libraries LVGL, ArduinoJson, noise-c and
# libsodium (libdeps/), the PlatformIO platform native and tool-scons
# (pio-core/), Tessera at the pinned commit, the folder tessera/ of
# tsx-xx50-linux, the folder panel-app/esphome of tsx-linux-common, and every
# license text (LICENSE, NOTICE, licenses/). ESPHome itself does not run here:
# it needs Python modules with Rust and C parts that Alpine armv7 does not
# have as wheels.
#
# build() compiles the project with compile.sh of the archive: PlatformIO and
# the g++, libdrm and libjpeg-turbo of Alpine. PlatformIO $_pio and its Python
# dependencies are the wheels in source= (exact versions, all py3-none-any),
# installed with pip --no-index. compile.sh takes the libraries and the
# platform from the archive. So the build needs no network.
# Testing: a commit archive of tsx-xx50-linux has no generated project, so a
# test build uses the pre-release tag v<next>_pre<YYYYMMDD> of tsx-xx50-linux
# (docs/build.md "Test builds" of that repo). The release <next> on main uses
# the tag v$pkgver again, with tsx-xx50-board>=$pkgver.
# 0.3.7: the program reads the release notes of tsx-autoupdate 0.3.7 (a newline
# is the two characters \n in update.state).
# 0.3.8: no touch poll, and the entities send a change only.
# 0.3.10: the sensor "Last boot".
# 0.3.11_pre20261028: Tessera (testing). Any standby counts as a dark screen
# for tsx-autoupdate. tsx-xx50-board 0.3.10 is enough: Tessera needs no new
# board file. The package installs every license text, and the build needs no
# network.
pkgname=tsx-xx50-panel-app
pkgver=0.3.11_pre20261028
pkgrel=0
_pio=6.1.19
pkgdesc="TSX panel app program for the xx50 panels (Tessera, ESPHome, LVGL, DRM/KMS)"
url="https://github.com/tsx-mainline/tsx-xx50-linux"
arch="armv7"
# Tessera is AGPL-3.0-or-later ("version 3 of the License or (at your option)
# any later version", NOTICE of Tessera). The C++ code of ESPHome is GPL-3.0
# (the ESPHome License says GPLv3, with no "or any later version"). The
# program combines the two under section 13 of both licenses: each part keeps
# its license, and the network terms of AGPL section 13 apply to the whole
# program. The program also contains the tsx-linux-common components
# (GPL-2.0-or-later), LVGL, ArduinoJson and noise-c (MIT), libsodium (ISC, the
# ESPHome port files MIT), the fonts Roboto and Noto Sans Symbols 2 (OFL-1.1)
# and Material Design Icons (Apache-2.0).
license="AGPL-3.0-or-later AND GPL-3.0-only AND GPL-2.0-or-later AND MIT AND ISC AND OFL-1.1 AND Apache-2.0"
# tsx_drm draws with libdrm (no SDL, no EGL). The live camera view decodes
# JPEG pictures with libjpeg-turbo.
depends="tsx-panel-app>=0.3.6 tsx-xx50-board>=0.3.10 libdrm libjpeg-turbo libstdc++"
makedepends="build-base libdrm-dev libjpeg-turbo-dev python3 py3-pip"
options="!check !fhs"
_srcurl="https://github.com/tsx-mainline/tsx-xx50-linux/releases/download/v$pkgver/tsx-xx50-panel-app-src-$pkgver.tar.gz"
# PlatformIO $_pio and its dependencies, as pip resolves them for the Python
# of Alpine v3.24 (pip download platformio==$_pio).
_pypi=https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages
